== L06 twin docstring claim about printed cents (lines 3-6)
Every number is exact. Shares, bond positions and prices are Fraction values. Prices
are printed in integer cents (half up, which changes nothing here because every price
is already a whole number of cents). Shares and bond positions are printed as exact
fractions in currency units, because they are positions, not prices. The parameters are model
== L06 printed output lines that show prices in currency units (no cents suffix)
133:        <p>Let \(f\) be the payoff at expiry, so the claim pays \(f(S(N,k))\) at node \((N, k)\). Define \(V(N,k) = f(S(N,k))\) and, for \(n < N\),</p>
167:        <p class="hypothesis">Stated before running: with spot 100, strike 100, up factor 3/2, down factor 1/2 and gross return 5/4 per period, the one-period price by replication equals the discounted risk-neutral expectation, 30 (3000 cents). The two-period price by backward induction equals the closed-form path sum, 45 (4500 cents). A self-financing strategy constructed from the one-period replications reproduces each node value and each payoff at expiry. Expected result: the output shows these equalities; the one-period check, the four path checks and the self-financing check print True. All inputs are model values; no data are read.</p>
